      "observed": "The SMC MCU option U3 is an ATtiny13V-10S, and its VCC (pin 8) is connected directly to the +5V rail generated by U1 (LM1117-5.0). The ATtiny13V variant is specified for VCC = 1.8–3.6 V only, yet the rail it sits on is 5 V (the same rail that also carries the 5.1 V TACH clamp zener D1 and the +5V pull-ups R3/R6, confirming the MCU supply is intended to be 5 V).",
      "expected": "On a 5 V supply the SMD footprint should be populated with a 5 V-rated part (ATtiny13-10S), consistent with the THT option U2 = ATtiny45-20P (1.8–5.5 V). A 'V'-suffix device must not be tied to +5V.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "U3 ATtiny13V-10S ; pin 8 VCC -> +5V (sheet /, right tile, column 6 row C)"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "U1 LM1117-5.0 ; pin 3 V0 -> +5V ; D1 5V1 ; R6 10K to VCC (sheet /, tiles)"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "U2 ATtiny45-20P ; pin 8 VCC -> +5V (sheet /, right tile, column 6 row B)"}
      ],
      "impact": "If the SMD variant (U3) is assembled, the microcontroller is powered above its maximum recommended VCC, giving out-of-spec / unreliable operation and risk of latch-up or permanent damage; the board would not behave as the 5 V design intends.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C2", "U1"],
      "pins": ["U1.3", "C2.1"],
      "nets": ["+5V"],
      "observed": "The only capacitor shown on the LM1117-5.0 output (+5V, pin 3) is C2 = 100 nF; there is no bulk (≈10 µF) output capacitor anywhere on the +5V rail.",
      "expected": "The LM1117 datasheet requires a low-ESR output capacitor of at least ~10 µF for loop stability; 100 nF alone is far below the specified minimum and the regulator will oscillate.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "U1 LM1117-5.0 ; C2 100nF on +5V (sheet /, right tile, column 6 row A)"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "C1 100nF on VCC ; C2 100nF on +5V (sheet /, left tile, column 5 row A)"}
      ],
      "impact": "Insufficient output capacitance makes the LDO unstable, producing oscillation / noise on the 5 V rail that powers the MCU and the I2C/ISP connectors.",
      "confidence": 0.3
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic is internally consistent for a 5 V fan controller (5.1 V TACH zener, +5V pull-ups, 5 V regulator), but the SMD MCU option U3 is an ATtiny13V-10S (1.8–3.6 V part) tied to the +5V rail, which is a rating violation; additionally the LM1117-5.0 output has only a 100 nF capacitor instead of the required ~10 µF, a stability deviation."
}

